<title>USA: DuPont Merck names Howes CEO.</title>
<headline>DuPont Merck names Howes CEO.</headline>
<dateline>WILMINGTON, Del. 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>DuPont Merck said on Monday that Paul Howes has been appointed president and chief executive officer of DuPont Merck effective December 16, 1996.</p>
<p>Howes will succeed Kurt Landgraf who was recently elected chief financial officer and member of the office of the chief executive of DuPont, said the company, which is a partnership between DuPont Co and Merck &amp; Co Inc.</p>
<p>For the past three years, Howes has been president of Merck Frosst, the Canadian business unit of Merck &amp; Co, DuPont Merck said.</p>
</text>
